      "id": "6fcc938e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "You can see that in the lasso case, many coefficients are exactly $0$. This is one reason lasso is often viewed as performing both regularization and variable selection.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Coefficient paths\n",
        "\n",
        "To better understand how the regularization parameter affects the estimates, we now plot the coefficient paths.\n",
        "\n",
        "- In the lasso plot, some coefficient curves hit exactly $0$ as `alpha` increases.\n",
        "- In the ridge plot, all coefficients are shrunk continuously toward $0$, but usually remain nonzero.\n"
      ],
      "id": "7291c005"
